      "title": "Write-ahead log",
      "type": "row"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "mimir"
      },
      "description": "A flat plateau is healthy: the WAL is at its high-water mark and being reused in place. A line that RISES AND DOES NOT PLATEAU means a writer is starving on the write lock right now -- it will spin in withDie's ~83 min retry budget before throwing, and the WAL absorbs every write in the meantime. Only the periodic leiosDbGarbageCollect maintenance call (checkpoint-only; it no longer evicts rows) runs wal_checkpoint(TRUNCATE), and it first fires once the immutable tip starts advancing, so nothing reclaims the high-water mark before then.\n\nOn 2026-08-06 node1 rode this to 5.7 GB against a 2.3 GB database.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "axisBorderShow": false,
